.TH PINBOARD 1
.SH NAME
pinboard \- window manager desktop and application launcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wm/pinboard
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Pinboard
provides a frameless desktop surface for
.IR wm (1).
It remains below ordinary application windows and displays icons for files,
directories, and RISC OS-style application directories.
The standard
.IR toolbar (1)
initialisation script starts one pinboard and places a selection of applications
on it.
.PP
An application directory has a name beginning with
.B !
and contains a
.B !Boot
file.
It normally also contains a
.B !Run
script and an
.BI icons/ name .bit
image, with an optional matching
.B .mask
file.
When such a directory is activated,
.I pinboard
forks a private process group, file descriptor group, name space, and
environment; sets
.B approot
and, when an icon is present,
.BR wmicon ;
applies
.BR !Boot ;
and executes
.BR !Run .
Application activation does not pass through the plumber.
.PP
Activating any other pinned path sends a text message to
.IR plumber (8).
The message source is
.BR pinboard ,
its directory is the directory containing the path,
and its data is the complete path.
The applicable rule in
.IR plumbing (6)
determines what opens the object.
.SS Pointer operations
.TP
.B Button 1 on an icon
Select the icon.  Dragging moves it; if it belongs to a multiple selection,
dragging moves the entire selection.
.TP
.B Button 1 on empty space
Clear the selection.
.TP
.B Button 3 drag on empty space
Rubber-band a group of icons into the selection.
.TP
.B Button 2
Open the context menu.  Its operations remove selected icons, clear the
backdrop, or tidy all icons into a grid.
.TP
.B Double button 1 on an icon
Activate the pinned object as described above.
.PP
Icon positions and the backdrop are held in memory.
They are not automatically preserved when the pinboard exits, but the complete
state can be read from and restored through
.BR /chan/pinboard ;
see
.IR pinboard (4).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /chan/pinboard
Textual control and state interface.
.TP
.B /lib/wmsetup
Starts the pinboard and supplies its initial icons.
.TP
.BI /Apps/! name /!Boot
Application name-space description.
.TP
.BI /Apps/! name /!Run
Application launch script.
.TP
.BI /Apps/! name /icons/! name .bit
Application icon, optionally accompanied by a
.B .mask
file.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/wm/pinboard.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR wm (1),
.IR toolbar (1),
.IR pinboard (4),
.IR plumbing (6),
.IR plumber (8)
.SH BUGS
Paths containing spaces cannot be represented by the current
.B /chan/pinboard
protocol.

